                    "stringValue": "[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"An **agent trace** is a record of what an AI agent did during a task, step by step. It may include the agent\u2019s inputs, observations, tool calls, tool results, and final response.\\n\\nFor example:\\n\\n1. User asks for the weather.\\n2. Agent calls a weather tool.\\n3. Tool returns the forecast.\\n4. Agent reports the forecast to the user.\\n\\nTraces are useful for debugging, auditing, and evaluating an agent. They don\u2019t necessarily include the model\u2019s private internal reasoning; often they show only observable actions and results.\"}],\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}]"
